[#:seon.task{:name "run-answers-a-whole-namespace-without-a-verdict"
             :kind :function
             :intent "(`my.test/run`) in seon.render.value-test ran all 52 members to test one new deftest: over 30 s, past MCP's default bound, which answered only a timeout with no handle (the run finished and recorded at 22:04:14). Its answer is a vector of 52 per-test maps in symbol order, so the shown text starts with green members and the one red test is cut. Answer passed?, counts and the red members first (`seon.test/tally`'s verdict) and accept a named test or the tests naming a task, as `my.test/check` does for changes."
             :must-read #{my.test/run-owned seon.test/tally}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/repl-dogfood-2026-09-27.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "run-owned-reply-repeats-its-output"
             :kind :function
             :intent "`my.test/run-owned` answers about 800 tokens for one test, with a duplicated :out. Done when the reply is focused through the render (one output, the verdict, the failing assertions' data) and its token size is asserted in a regression."
             :must-read #{my.test/run-owned}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-08/task-census/evidence/repl-audit--change.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "test-output-and-an-empty-reaching-run-reach-the-reply"
             :kind :function
             :intent "A `my.test/check` reply carries clojure.test's \"Testing ns\" (and FAIL) lines in `:out`, printed outside the value printer; and the automatic test step reports `:seon.turn.loop/reaching {:seon.test/passed? false :seon.turn.loop/red []}` after an eval request on a fresh agent branch with no change (both observed on default 2026-10-08, agent integrate-2-probe). A one-test check there allocated 2.5 GB in 1.67 s. Done when the report reaches the agent only as data and a reaching run with nothing to run says so instead of `passed? false`. (The pilot's other half, a test named as changed being refused, no longer reproduces.)"
             :must-read #{my.test/check seon.test/run seon.turn/run-reaching}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-08/dogfood/pilot.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "check-ignores-the-tests-key"
             :kind :function
             :intent "(my.test/check {:seon.test/tests [sym]}) ignores the key and runs the tests reaching the named function instead (13 s) (PB-15 dogfood run, lane dogfood-pb15, default, 2026-10-08). Done when a named test list runs exactly those tests, with a regression, or the request schema refuses the key."
             :must-read #{my.test/check}}
 #:seon.task{:name "an-agent-cannot-run-one-test-by-hand"
             :kind :function
             :intent "At an agent's REPL (clojure.test/run-test-var #'t) throws ClassCastException (sci.lang.Namespace cannot be cast to clojure.lang.Symbol), (clojure.test/run-test t) and (clojure.test/test-vars [#'t]) answer nil, and calling the deftest prints FAIL lines located at (lookup.clj:43) (fanout run, default e1a71b7c8, 2026-10-08; agents fan-source and live-flash-4 tried these). Done when clojure.test's own run-test-var and run-test answer their summary map at the agent's REPL, as in Clojure. Reproduced again on default caba650fa (agent chain-frictions-probe, 2026-10-10): (ns cf.scratch (:require [clojure.test :as t])) (t/deftest cf-t (t/is true)) (t/run-test-var #'cf-t) throws \"class sci.lang.Namespace cannot be cast to class clojure.lang.Symbol\" (1 ms). Same class as `seon.sci.eval` task run-test-var-throws-on-an-sci-test-var, whose proof this task shares."
             :must-read #{my.test/run-owned}}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-two-test-check-allocates-a-gigabyte-and-a-half"
             :kind :function
             :intent "(`my.test/check` {:seon.test/changed ['seon.db/registered-attribute-candidates 'seon.db/missing-connection-error]}) at root ran two reaching tests whose run-ms were 40 and 22 ms but took 1,395 ms and allocated 1,419 MB (fanout-3 run, default 324461975, 2026-10-09); a check reaching nothing (my.test/check-now) took 186 ms and 311 MB. Done when a check's cost follows the tests it runs, its allocation owners named by `seon.profile/measure`."
             :must-read #{my.test/check seon.test/run}}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-check-failure-shows-no-message"
             :kind :function
             :intent "`my.test/check` rendered an errored test as only `{:seon.test/sym ...}` under `:seon.render.test/failures` (lane repl-only-a5, 2026-10-09); its message, \"The admitted identity has no executable test Var.\", was found three evaluations later under `:seon.test/results` `:seon.test.failure/reports`. Done when each listed failure shows its report message."
             :must-read #{my.test/check}}]
